## 6. Security, resilience & testing

**Server validation:** `[Required]`, `[StringLength]`, `[Range]`, custom image/time-limit validators, MVC `ModelState`, ownership/role checks and quiz/domain constraints. Incorrect submissions should not persist changes.

**Client validation:** MVC jQuery Validation + Unobtrusive adapters handle supported Data Annotation rules. The custom `question-form-validation.js` checks options, duplicates, correct answers and accepted short answers. `register-validation.js` checks the registration modal/standard form's username/password and confirmation logic. The image preview checks MIME type and 5 MiB maximum. Client checks are feedback only and can be bypassed.

**Error handling and security:** Identity provides login/session management; `[Authorize]` and ownership checks protect sensitive actions. `AccountController.AccessDenied` sets 403. Serilog writes structured errors and request context; repositories log database exceptions and rethrow. The former `Authentication/ValidateUserCookieEvents.cs` is **legacy and not registered** with the current Identity configuration. A Development-only cookie revalidation change was reviewed but deliberately deferred; no claim of instant cookie invalidation following reseeding is made.

**Tests:** 72 automated backend cases passed with zero failed/skipped on the test commit. Positive scenarios include valid challenge title/description lengths, supported time limits, valid question points, valid login/registration, saved challenge creation, and successful personal image listing. Negative scenarios include empty/overlong fields, invalid time limits, invalid question points, invalid/duplicate answers, rejected quiz attempts, unauthorized challenge edits, missing image deletion, and repository save failures. These provide more than six examples of each kind across xUnit facts and inline-data theories.

**CI:** `.github/workflows/build.yml` runs the Release build, checks JavaScript syntax with Node, and runs the xUnit project. This does **not** replace browser or full integration tests.

**Manual testing still required and NOT claimed completed:** Browser smoke-test CRUD for each entity; login/roles; server rejection with client scripts bypassed; network/console and antiforgery behavior; default and personal image upload/delete; mobile layout; friendly errors; time limits; form-validation messages; error-log correlation. **[TEAM: record screenshots, environment, date, results and defects.]**

